-- title:
--   Evaluate all graph-sketch layers for one fixed random trial
-- statement:
--   Let $k\ge1$ and let the native base state be ready for a graph's stored arc list: graph headers, unary templates and arc records are initialized, and all computation scratch stacks are empty. Load a prescribed trial bit string $\omega$ into the cached-sign state, decoding labels $\sigma$ and sketch signs $R$. The graph-layers program replaces the empty previous-layer database by
--   $$
--   \bigl(\operatorname{denseLayer}(k,v,a)\bigr)_{v<n,\,a<k}
--   $$
--   as framed arrays in vertex-major, state-minor order. Apart from this database, the entire labeled state is preserved. Its running time is at most
--   $$
--   C_{\rm first}(n,k)+C_{\rm layers}(n,k,m),
--   $$
--   where the first term is the verified first-layer budget and the second is the verified driver budget for the remaining $k-1$ layers, with $m$ stored arcs. This is the full exterior-DP stage of a trial.
-- source:
--   T. Koana, Approximate Counting of k-Paths in O*(2^k) Time, STOC 2027 submission #953, October 2026, §3.2 (printed pp. 8–9 / PDF pp. 9–10) and §4.1 (printed p. 9 / PDF p. 10), https://github.com/sigact-stoc/stoc2027/releases/download/papers-2/953.pdf. Native implementation: Solutions/GraphLayers.lean, line 19; source snapshot SHA-256 a6ddb9a180723e03cc2805157309bca42456b0503887eef9fe691a4fa9cd3fa0.

